  Color-coded: blue = commercial elements, green = defense elements.

Figure 3 — Conceptual ZT 5G defense architecture:
  UE (SDP IH) --5G/PLMN--> gNB (commercial) --> CN (SDP AH, military CP+UP)
  CN <==SDP control channel==> 5G Military ZT Manager (SDP controller)
  CN <==SDP data channel==> ZT Manager

Figure 4 — End-to-end communication/data flow (the paper's main
process/sequence diagram, functionally a DFD):
  Actors: UE (SDP IH) | Commercial gNB | CN (SDP AH) | 5G Military ZT
  Manager (SDP controller) | Server (SDP IH)
  Flow:
  1. Preparation: ZT manager pre-registers/provisions subscribers+devices;
     sets up secure control channels with CN and server.
  2. CN <--auth--> ZT manager: authorized & secure SDP control channel.
  3. Server <--auth--> ZT manager: authorized & secure SDP control channel.
  4. ZT manager --(UE info for 5G comms)--> CN.
  5. Standard 5G session: UE selects military PLMN ID via gNB → 5G
     authentication with CN → 5G data channel established.
  6. CN --(ready-UE info)--> ZT manager.
  7. Data-channel-to-private-network phase: UE <--auth--> ZT manager over
     SDP control channel → ZT manager --(accepted IH info)--> CN →
     SDP data channel opened between UE and private network resources.

