  Step 4: UPF iptables (SDP ON) -> "anywhere" ACCEPT rule added for the
          authenticated UE's IP (12.1.1.2)
  Step 5: UE to web server, 5G ON / SDP ON -> access SUCCEEDS

================================================================
* METHODS (attack scenarios & measurement techniques)
================================================================
- DoS attack test: single attacker node (UE 0) floods the server with
  high-volume TCP traffic; SDP data-channel sessions are torn down if an
  authenticated IH fails to send a keep-alive within 3 seconds.
  Measured: average network throughput over a 30-second window under
  4 conditions (SDP on/off × attack on/off).
- IP scanning test: attacker UE runs `nmap -e uesimtun0 -sn
  192.168.56.0/24` to enumerate live hosts.
  Measured: number of discoverable hosts/services with SDP off vs. on.
- Connection-time measurement: time for a 5G terminal to establish a data
  connection, with vs. without SDP, averaged over 10 iterations; compared
  against reference values from [32].
- Real-world verification: manual step-through of UE access attempts
  before/after SDP authentication, inspecting UPF iptables rule changes
  and SDP IH/AH/controller logs and GUI.

