================================================================
* CONCLUSION
================================================================
The paper demonstrates a practical way to integrate 5G into a defense
network using a mix of commercial and military-specific components under
a Zero Trust architecture. Using a commercial gNB with a military PLMN ID,
paired with an SDP-based ZT layer managed by a dedicated military ZT
manager, the authors show — via simulation and a real-world testbed —
that the design mitigates IP-scanning and DoS attacks while keeping
authentication and access control strictly enforced, even over an active
5G radio connection. The results support commercial-5G-based military
networks as a viable, lower-cost, higher-coverage alternative to
fully isolated private 5G networks, without giving up ZT-grade security.
